3/2609.02 held above 2604.75 for eight bars to 2700.00 (bar 116 high); the last raw close 2577.06 is still above the H4 pre-breakout top 2544.63 (context, not a vote).", "The M15 pullback came back to the prior H1 breakout base and held: M15 bar 109 (open_time 1789874100000) low 2569.8 versus H1 bar 81 (open_time 1789743600000) low 2569.16 and high 2585.5; H1 bar 117 (open_time 1789873200000) open 2572.94, low 2569.8, close 2586.68 - a bull reversal bar closing back above 2585.5.", "After the M15 bear spike bar 107 (open 2603.75, low 2571, close 2573.13) there is no new low: bars 108 and 109 set 2570.27 and 2569.8, and the last three lows are 2574.41 (bar 117), 2573.82 (bar 118), 2574.18 (bar 119) with no close below 2573.13 - a double bottom that keeps holding.", "M15 bar 119 (open_time 1789883100000) open 2574.40, high 2577.99, low 2574.18, close 2577.06 is a bull reversal bar closing near its high that reverses bar 118's bear bar (open 2577.21, low 2573.82, close 2574.40) at the low of the 12-bar range 2569.8-2594.57.", "Location and equation: the pending stop sits in the lower third of a 24.77-point tight range, 8.19 above the structural low 2569.8, while the first resistance at 2594.57 (bars 108/109 high) is 16.58 away."], "evidence_against": ["Strongest counter: the large recent bars are bear breakouts that broke structure - M15 bar 107 (open 2603.75, low 2571, close 2573.13) and H1 bar 116 (open 2617.83, low 2571, close 2573.13) closed near their lows well below the H1/H4 7-bar range low 2604.75, so the 12-bar M15 range is at least as easily read as a bear flag, and the first reversal attempt after such a spike often fails with a second leg down.", "The range's highs keep falling: 2594.57 (bars 108/109), 2587.03 (110), 2586.73 (112), 2585.39 (113), 2583.44 (116/117), 2580.56 (118), 2577.99 (119) - the 2577.99 trigger must clear three lower highs before the 2594.57 top is even tested.", "H1 bar 119 (open 2578.56, low 2573.82, close 2577.06) closed below H1 bar 118's low 2578.33, so the newest H1 close is bearish and under the prior bar's low; the H4 context's last close 2586.68 predates these two H1 closes.", "H4 context flags a buy climax: bar 116's 2700.00 exceeded 2680.00 by only 20.00 and closed 61.51 below its high, and its final bar closed under the 7-bar range low 2604.75 and under the lows of bars 113-119; this long is the first pullback of a possibly unconfirmed MTR, with 2537.57-2544.63 as deeper support.", "The entry is not the range's extreme low (2569.8) and no bull breakout above 2594.57 has occurred, so the stop can be filled while the 12-bar range is still undecided."], "qualitative_confidence": "low", "uncertainty": ["The 12-bar M15 range 2569.8-2594.57 has not resolved; a break below 2569.8 (bear flag) and a break above 2594.57 (bull flag) are both live.", "The buy stop at 2577.99 is pending and untriggered at the 2577.06 close; if price closes below 2569.8 first the setup is void.", "The H4 context's content ends at the H1 bar 117 close 2586.68 (as-of 1789876799999) and excludes H1 bars 118-119 (closes 2580.35, 2577.06), so its bullish 'final close above 2585.50' point is older than the raw bars.", "The 2700.00 buy climax with a 61.51 upper tail raises the chance the pullback extends toward 2537.57-2544.63 before any resumption, which would invalidate this entry even if the larger trend stays up."], "conditions_that_change_market_read": ["An M15 close below 2569.8 (bar 109 low) breaks the pullback's double bottom and voids the long; next references are the H4 pre-breakout top 2544.63/2537.57 and then 2495.82.", "Acceptance above 2594.57 (bars 108/109 high) confirms the range as a bull flag and puts 2604.75 and 2643.52 in play.", "Two consecutive M15 closes below 2569.8 would confirm the bear flag and shift the read toward the H4 range breakdown described in the H4 transition conditions.", "If price makes a lower high under 2577.99 and closes below 2573.82 (bar 118 low) without triggering, the bull signal is stale and the 12-bar range reads as a bear flag."]}, "latest_trader_intent": {"schema": "brooks.trade-intent.v2", "role": "TRADER", "decision": "NO_TRADE", "symbol": "ETH-USDT", "decision_time_ms": 1789887599999, "market_context": {"M15_state": "16-bar tight range 2569.80-2594.57 (bear flag) directly under the two-bar bear spike of M15 bars 102-103", "H1_state": "lower-high sequence off 2658.79 (H1 bar 106, open_time 1789837200000) into 2583.54 (H1 bar 119); last H1 bar closed at the decision time on the 2569.80-2570 shelf", "H4_regime": "bull-trend/channel per current context, but bar 120 (O 2632.98, C 2586.68) closed below the 2604.75 low of the seven-bar range; 2700.00 reversal unconfirmed", "D1_regime": "bull-trend inside a post-buy-climax range 2357.18-2771.00; price is near the ~2564 midpoint", "location": "bottom edge of the M15 range, middle of the D1 range, above the H4 pre-breakout top 2537.57-2544.63"}, "setup": {"type": "tight trading range after a two-bar bear spike (bear flag), not yet broken", "trigger_status": "absent", "signal_quality": "weak", "location_assessment": "poor", "no_trade_reason": "poor_location"}, "decision_timeframe": null, "context_timeframes_used": ["M15", "H1", "H4", "D1"], "entry_mechanism": "none", "trigger": null, "invalidation": null, "evidence_for": ["M15 bars 102-103 (open_time 1789871400000 and 1789872300000) are the bear leg: bar 103 opens 2603.75, high 2606.04, low 2571, close 2573.13; the following 16 bars (bar 104 high 2594.57 to bar 119 low 2570.00) all overlap inside 2569.80-2594.57, i.e. the market is in a tight trading range, not a trending leg, so the environment Brooks treats as no-trade until it breaks applies.", "The 2569.80-2571.00 shelf has been defended four times: M15 bar 104 low 2570.27, bar 105 low 2569.80, bar 118 low 2570.35, bar 119 low 2570.00. Selling a stop below that shelf would be selling the fourth defence of the same level, at the bottom edge of the range, which is a poor location.", "The decision bar, M15 bar 119 (open_time 1789886700000, close_time 1789887599999; O 2571.76, H 2574.94, L 2570.00, C 2574.06), is an inside bar relative to bar 118 (H 2581.12, L 2570.35) with a lower low and a close only 0.88 under its high; it is not a decisive signal bar in either direction.", "H1 bars show a lower-high sequence with no trend-acceleration: highs 2658.79 (H1 bar 106, open_time 1789837200000), 2636.47 (H1 bar 112, open_time 1789858800000), 2586.73 (H1 bar 118, open_time 1789876800000) and 2583.54 (H1 bar 119, open_time 1789884000000), while the last H1 bar low 2570 holds just above the prior low 2569.80; this is a bear roll-over pressed onto support, not a clean breakout either way.", "Location versus the larger context: the D1 range is 2357.18-2771.00 with midpoint about 2564, so 2574.06 sits in the middle of the dominant D1 range, and the current H4 context still classifies the regime as a bull channel with the 2700.00 reversal marked unconfirmed; both the short (counter to H4/D1 Always-In long) and the long (under a two-bar bear spike) are crowded."], "evidence_against": ["Strongest counterargument for a short: a two-bar bear spike followed by a 16-bar tight range is a textbook bear flag, and H4 bar 120 (open_time 1789862400000, O 2632.98, C 2586.68) already closed below the 2604.75 low of its seven-bar range, so a pending stop below 2569.80 (M15 bar 105 low) with invalidation above 2583.54 (M15 bar 117 high) is a defined, actionable structure even before it triggers.", "Strongest counterargument for a long: D1 and H4 are Always-In long with rising swing lows, the M15 pullback is still above the H4 pre-breakout top 2537.57-2544.63, and bar 119 closing 2574.06 near its high at a four-times-tested shelf is a small bull reversal that a bull-flag entry could be built on.", "The last two M15 highs (2583.54 bar 117, 2581.12 bar 118) failed but never closed below the shelf, so an outright bear continuation is unproven and could equally be a failed breakdown into a bull-flag launch."], "qualitative_confidence": "medium", "uncertainty": ["Whether the 16-bar M15 range resolves as a bear flag (continuation of H4 bar 120's break below 2604.75) or as a bull flag inside the H4 channel is unresolved at the decision bar.", "Whether H4's 2700.00 marginal new high (20.00 above 2680.00) is an unconfirmed lower high / MTR or a pause before another bull leg.", "Whether the 2569.80 shelf holds or breaks: bar 119's low 2570.00 leaves the level intact by only 0.20, so the test is unresolved rather than failed."], "conditions_that_change_market_read": ["An M15 close below 2569.80 (M15 bar 105 low) with follow-through would confirm the bear-flag breakdown and make a stop short with invalidation above 2583.54 (M15 bar 117 high) actionable.", "An M15 close above 2594.57 (M15 bars 104-105 equal high) with follow-through would confirm an upward resolution of the range and re-align the M15 with the H4/D1 bull trend.", "A bull reversal bar closing back above 2583.54 with a higher low would keep the H4 bull channel read and convert the shelf into a launch point.", "An H4 close below 2495.82 (H4 bar 111 low) would end the higher-low sequence and confirm the reversal case, shifting the read away from bull-trend."]}, "latest_market_context": {"schema": "brooks.market-context.v1", "role": "HTF_ANALYST", "symbol": "ETH-USDT", "decision_time_ms": 1789862399999, "timeframe": "D1", "observations": ["120 closed D1 bars, open_time 1779494400000 to 1789776000000, with the decision at the close of the final bar (close_time 1789862399999).", "Window high is 2771 (bar 90, open_time 1787270400000); window low is 1368.42 (bar 14, open_time 1780704000000).", "Bars 10-14 (1780358400000-1780704000000) are five overlapping bear bars driving 2006.17 down to 1368.42; bar 14 closes 1568.55, about 200 points above its low, a sell-climax tail.", "Bar 88 (1787097600000) opens 1916.51 inside the prior consolidation and closes 2252.16 near its 2293.8 high; bars 89-90 close 2326.32 and 2515.3, and bar 90 prints 2771 and closes 255.7 below that high.", "Bars 91-119 overlap between 2357.18 (bar 102 low, 1788307200000) and 2700 (bar 119 high); bar 90's low of 2325.31 was never revisited.", "Roughly equal lows at 2357.18 (bar 102) and 2358.62 (bar 115, 1789430400000) form a double bottom at the range low, followed by four higher closes (2416.57, 2446.22, 2612.02, 2632.98).", "The final bar's close 2632.98 is the highest close in the whole window, while its high 2700 stays 71 below bar 90's 2771 high; the last bar closes 67.02 under its own high."], "evidence_against": ["Bar 90's 2771 high with a close 255.7 lower is a buy-climax bar, and the 29 bars since then overlap inside the range rather than trending - trading-range behavior after a climax.", "No close has exceeded 2771; the recent highs 2680 (bar 111) and 2700 (bar 119) are below the spike high, so the range top has already rejected the bulls.", "Bar 115 fell from 2517.53 to 2358.62 in a single bar, showing fast two-sided movement inside the range and poor trend persistence.", "The final bar closed 67.02 below its own 2700 high, so there is no acceptance yet at the upper boundary; the bull push is an in-range leg, not a confirmed breakout.", "The 2357.18 and 2358.62 lows are roughly equal, which marks a range floor that has been tested twice and can break rather than hold."], "uncertainty": ["V2 D1 context adapted for the V1 PM input."]}, "management_history": [{"schema": "brooks.management-decision.v2", "role": "POSITION_MANAGER", "decision_time_ms": 1789884959999, "action": "HOLD", "position_ids": ["wf-main-1"], "reason": "State is coherent: one MAIN LONG 0.604 ETH (wf-main-1), hedge_state single_main/unresolved=false, margin_health SAFE, and the documented invalidation at 2569.80 is still unbroken on closed M15 bars. management_policy has strategy_stop_required=false, so the empty open_orders book is policy-compliant and no forced protection action applies. The recorded breakout-pullback premise is challenged but not contradicted: the latest closed M15 bar (close_time 1789884899999) opened 2577.06, held 2573.80, and closed 2577.70, above the 2569.80 double-bottom low and above the entry 2578.33's structural reference, with no close below the 2573.13 bear-spike close. Holding keeps the existing exposure and the executor-configured stop 2569.80 / target 2594.61 intact rather than realizing a loss into an undecided 12-bar range.", "evidence": {"observations": ["Position wf-main-1: ETH-USDT LONG 0.604, entry 2578.327807, mark 2578.07, unrealized PnL -0.1557, ownership_role MAIN, as_of 1789884959999; equity 9999.2214, available margin 9687.7905, margin_health SAFE.", "hedge_state: structure_status single_main, unresolved false, main_size 0.604, hedge_size 0, hedge_ratio 0, net_exposure_usd 1557.15428, gross_exposure_usd 1557.15428, main_position_id wf-main-1.", "executor_state (as_of 1789884959999): executor wf-exec-1 status RUNNING, position_id wf-main-1, config stop_price 2569.80, target_price 2594.61, matching the intent invalidation (2569.80) and first resistance (2594.57).", "open_orders is empty; recent_fills has only wf-fill-1 (0.604 LONG at 2578.327807, fee 0.622924); fills_since_last_event is empty, so no unaccounted quantity change or partial fill.", "management_policy brooks-pm-v1: strategy_stop_required=false, allowed actions include HOLD; semantics state PM decisions are advisory and only the deterministic GM writes to the venue.", "Latest 10 closed M15 bars (last close_time 1789884899999): range highs fall 2586.73, 2585.39, 2584.59, 2583.44, 2583.44, 2580.56, 2577.99; lows 2574.41, 2573.82, 2574.18, 2573.80 with no close below 2573.13; final bar 2577.06/2578.05/2573.80/2577.70."], "evidence_for": ["The documented premise (breakout_pullback long, invalidation 2569.80) is unchallenged at the invalidation level: every one of the last four closed M15 lows (2574.41, 2573.82, 2574.18, 2573.80) sits above 2569.80, and no close is below th