ggered."], "qualitative_confidence": "medium", "uncertainty": ["The 2850.00 print on M15 bar 110 is not corroborated by any other individual supplied bar; whether it is a genuine traded level or a data artifact is unknown.", "The trigger 2727.03 is untriggered, so the flag's resolution is unresolved at the decision time.", "Whether 2709.56-2727.03 is a bull flag (continuation) or the first pause before a deeper pullback to the 2700.00 breakout level cannot be settled from closed bars alone."], "conditions_that_change_market_read": ["Failure: an M15 close below 2709.56 followed by a close below 2700.00 would mark the breakout as failed and return the read to the 2358.62-2700.00 H4 range.", "Continuation: an M15 close above 2727.03 that holds above 2700.00 confirms the flag breakout and keeps focus on the 2850.00 spike high.", "Deeper damage: a close below 2656.75 (M15 bar 101 low, 1789974900000) would end the sequence of higher lows and put the bull leg in doubt."]}, "latest_market_context": {"schema": "brooks.market-context.v1", "role": "HTF_ANALYST", "symbol": "ETH-USDT", "decision_time_ms": 1789948799999, "timeframe": "D1", "observations": ["Window opens at 2116.86 and falls to 1368.42 (bar 13 low, close 1568.55), then reverses; final close 2642.90 is about +24.9% versus the first open and about +93% above the window low.", "Bars 87-89 are the spike: 1916.51 to 2252.16, 2252.20 to 2326.32, 2326.31 to 2515.30, with the window high 2771 printed on bar 89.", "Bars 90-116 are two-sided: overlapping bodies, highs at 2557.46 (bar 95) and 2609.02 (bar 113), lows clustered 2357.18-2425.44; bar 110 spiked to 2680 and closed 2514.72 back inside the range.", "Bars 117-119 close 2612.02, 2632.98, 2642.90 \u2014 the first consecutive closes above the 2557.46 ceiling; bar 117 has open 2446.22, high 2643.52, low 2436.87, range 206.65, closing in its top quarter; bar 118 reaches 2700.", "Bar 119 (open 2632.98, high 2645.88, low 2568.16, close 2642.90) is a 77.72-range bar closing