00, open 2734.92, high 2795, low 2730.01, close 2754.31) still holds above the 2700 breakout area (H1 bar 104 high 2700), so no trend break has occurred at the decision time."], "qualitative_confidence": "medium", "uncertainty": ["H4 context was stale at the snapshot and no raw H4 read was completed in this run, so structure above 2700 was read from raw H1/M15 bars rather than a fresh 120-bar H4 window.", "Bar 119 is a single M15 bar; its follow-through is outside the frozen window, so the breakout attempt is unresolved rather than failed.", "D1 context decision_time 1789948799999 predates the 2795 high, so its last close 2642.90 does not describe the current price."], "conditions_that_change_market_read": ["An M15 close above 2795 (bar 119 high) that keeps its low above 2743.84 would mark breakout acceptance above the 24-bar range and shift the read toward bull continuation.", "An M15 close below 2743.84 (bar 119 low), especially followed by a close below 2730, would flag rejection of the range-top breakout and open the 2718.09-2702.56 range base.", "Repeated M15 closes between 2747.76 and 2795 without a new high above 2795 would confirm a trading range at the highs (final-flag risk) rather than a breakout.", "A close below 2702.56 (M15 bar 94 low) would break the higher-low sequence running from the 2850 spike and support a failed-breakout read."]}, "latest_market_context": {"schema": "brooks.market-context.v1", "role": "HTF_ANALYST", "symbol": "ETH-USDT", "decision_time_ms": 1789948799999, "timeframe": "D1", "observations": ["Window opens at 2116.86 and falls to 1368.42 (bar 13 low, close 1568.55), then reverses; final close 2642.90 is about +24.9% versus the first open and about +93% above the window low.", "Bars 87-89 are the spike: 1916.51 to 2252.16, 2252.20 to 2326.32, 2326.31 to 2515.30, with the window high 2771 printed on bar 89.", "Bars 90-116 are two-sided: overlapping bodies, highs at 2557.46 (bar 95) and 2609.02 (bar 113), lows clustered 2357.18-2425.44; bar 110 spiked to 2680 and closed 2514.72 back inside the range.", "Bars 117-119 close 2612.02, 2632.98, 2642.90 \u2014 the first consecutive closes above the 2557.46 ceiling; bar 117 has open 2446.22, high 2643.52, low 2436.87, range 206.65, closing in its top quarter; bar 118 reaches 2700.", "Bar 119 (open 2632.98, high 2645.88, low 2568.16, close 2642.90) is a 77.72-range bar closing near its high while holding above the range ceiling; it makes a lower high than bar 118 (2645.88 vs 2700).", "Recent lows rise: 2357.18 (bar 101), 2358.62 (bar 114), 2370.54 (bar 115), 2413.82 (bar 116), 2436.87 (bar 117), 2568.16 (bar 119).", "Price 2642.90 remains below the bar-89 spike high 2771, so the post-spike section is not yet a confirmed new-high trend."], "evidence_against": ["The breakout is only three bars; the preceding 27 bars overlap heavily and the region 2357-2557 can still be read as the operating trading range rather than broken.", "Two earlier upside probes failed to hold: bar 110 high 2680 closed 2514.72, bar 113 high 2609.02 closed 2514.07, so upside spikes in this region have recently been rejected.", "2642.90 remains below the bar-89 spike high 2771, so the whole post-spike section can be read as one broad trading range whose upper extreme has not been exceeded.", "Bar 119 makes a lower high than bar 118 (2645.88 vs 2700) with a lower tail to 2568.16, a pause rather than a strong continuation bar, and bar 114 had just traded down to 2358.62 four bars before the breakout."], "uncertainty": ["V2 D1 context adapted for the V1 PM input."]}, "management_history": [{"schema": "brooks.management-decision.v2", "role": "POSITION_MANAGER", "decision_time_ms": 1790005679999, "action": "HOLD", "position_ids": ["wf-main-5"], "reason": "The snapshot is coherent: one MAIN LONG leg (wf-main-5, 0.159) matches the executor's position_id, hedge_state is single_main with no unresolved legs, margin_health is SAFE, and management_policy sets strategy_stop_required false, so th