pper tail); a stronger bull bar closing on its high would raise confidence in the same trigger.", "The D1 context is 15 hours older than the frozen decision time and its 2771/2557 levels are contextual descriptions; the D1 spike high 2771 was exceeded only by a wick (M15 bar 98 high 2850) with no close above it."], "conditions_that_change_market_read": ["A M15 close back below 2731.83 (bar 119 low) and then below 2718.09 (bar 117 low) would mark a failed breakout of the range high and void the long case.", "A M15/H1 close below 2702.56 (bar 98 low) would break the three-hour acceptance above the H4 2700 zone and return price to the prior H4 wide range.", "Repeated M15 closes between 2718.09 and 2747.76 without exceeding 2747.76 would keep the tight-range read and argue against a breakout.", "A M15 close above 2747.76 with the low holding above 2731.83 would confirm the breakout and shift the focus to 2771 and then 2850."]}, "latest_trader_intent": {"schema": "brooks.trade-intent.v2", "role": "TRADER", "decision": "ENTER_LONG", "symbol": "ETH-USDT", "decision_time_ms": 1790024399999, "market_context": {"primary_regime": "bull trend on H4/D1 in breakout-spike phase; M15 in a post-spike pause", "location": "close 2781.77 sits above the broken H4 range top 2700.00 and the D1 ceiling 2557.46, in the upper part of the M15 post-spike range (low of the pause 2734.22 to the leg high 2804.59), below the 2795.00 M15 spike high and the 2850.00 H4 spike high", "timeframe_alignment": "H4 and D1 context both always-in long; H1 closes rising (2740.89, 2756.61, 2760.51, 2781.77); M15 shows a two-bar inside-bar pause (ii) after bull bar 117", "strongest_opposite_case": "H4 bar 118 is a possible buy climax (range 191.94, upper tail 126.85 = 66% of range, close in lower third) and M15 bars 118-119 never exceeded bar 117's 2804.59 high, so a break below 2776.10 would mark a failed break above 2795.00 and shift the read to a deeper pullback toward 2734.22-2718.09"}, "setup": {"type": "co